---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# The dropWhile twin of `232-boxed-primitive-filter-to-filter` (#982), and the
# step that finally hands `310` the element type the issue asks for.
#
# By the time this fires, `208-lambda-to-primitive-dropwhile` has lifted the
# primitive call and `211` has wrapped it in the boxing sandwich it builds for
# every primitive operation — `Φ.hone.box`, the boxed pragma, `Φ.hone.unbox` —
# so the stream at this point carries `Ljava/lang/Integer;` while the predicate
# still takes the raw `I` that javac compiled it to take. That split is exactly
# what `232` writes out for a filter, and it is the whole answer to "how does
# the element type reach the fold": `bridge-input`/`bridge-output` name the
# BOXED element the fused body passes around, `accepted` names the PRIMITIVE the
# predicate wants, and `returned` matches `accepted` as it does on `p-filter`,
# because a dropWhile, like a filter, hands its item on untouched.
#
# `232` has to choose between `p-filter` and `o-filter` on the target's return
# type. This rule does not: `208`'s primitive sibling already refused anything
# whose target does not end in `)Z`, so the output is always the one
# Φ.hone.dropWhile name that `310` folds, and an `o-` variant that `310` could
# not lower can never be minted here.
#
# It sits at `233` rather than beside its producer because everything between
# `211` and here must see the pragma in its boxed form: `221` cancels the
# unbox/box pairs between adjacent primitive operations first, so a run of them
# ends up inside ONE sandwich, and `411` can then collapse that single pair back
# into a primitive distill. The parallel guard does NOT wait this long — `210`
# reverts the pragma before `211` boxes anything, so a parallel pipeline never
# reaches this rule at all.
name: boxed-primitive-dropwhile-to-dropwhile
pattern: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.boxed-primitive-dropWhile,
    opcode ↦ 𝑒-opcode,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    bridge-signature ↦ 𝑒-bridge-signature,
    static ↦ 𝑒-static,
    target ↦ ⟦
      𝐵-target-before,
      signature ↦ 𝑒-target-signature,
      𝐵-target-after
    ⟧
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.dropWhile,
    opcode ↦ 𝑒-opcode,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    bridge-input ↦ 𝑒-bridge-input,
    bridge-output ↦ 𝑒-bridge-input,
    accepted ↦ 𝑒-accepted,
    returned ↦ 𝑒-accepted,
    static ↦ 𝑒-static,
    target ↦ ⟦
      𝐵-target-before,
      signature ↦ 𝑒-target-signature,
      𝐵-target-after
    ⟧
  ⟧
where:
  - meta: 𝑒-bridge-input
    function: sed
    args:
      - 𝑒-bridge-signature
      - '"s/\\(I\\)Z/Ljava\\/lang\\/Integer;/g"'
      - '"s/\\(D\\)Z/Ljava\\/lang\\/Double;/g"'
      - '"s/\\(J\\)Z/Ljava\\/lang\\/Long;/g"'
  - meta: 𝑒-accepted
    function: sed
    args:
      - 𝑒-target-signature
      - '"s/\\((.+)\\).+/$1/g"'
